course: dictionary
lesson: 12141
title: Commuting: the same journey, day after day
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Commuting means travelling regularly between home and work or school. «Every morning, Dad commutes to the city by train.» The word tells you two things: the trip is made again and again, and it links home with work. If you can picture the same journey happening every day, you have the meaning.
explain: The noun commuting is the same idea as a thing: «Dad's commuting takes an hour each way.» Here commuting is the whole daily trip. You may also hear rush hour in the news: «Traffic was busy during the evening commute.» Look for words like every day, each morning or rush hour as clues.
explain: Commuting has two other meanings you may meet. In law, commuting a punishment means making it less severe. In maths, operations that commute give the same answer in either order. Use the words around the word to decide which meaning is right: a sentence about trains and work is about travel, while one about numbers is about maths.
fact: Commuting means travelling regularly between home and work or school.
fact: The verb forms are commute, commutes, commuted and commuting.
fact: «Commuting» is often used with words like train, bus, rush hour and traffic.
fact: In maths, adding commutes: 3 + 5 = 5 + 3, so the order does not change the answer.
fact: In law, commuting a punishment means making it less severe.
exercise: «Every day, Dad commutes to the city by train.» What does commutes mean? | Stays at home all day | *Travels regularly between home and work | Plays football at the weekend | Cooks dinner for the family
exercise: In maths, 3 + 5 = 5 + 3. Why is adding said to commute? | *The order can be swapped and the answer stays the same | It gets bigger each time | Needs a calculator to check | It always gives zero
exercise: Fill the gap: «Mum ___ to work by bus every day.» | *commutes | commute | commuted | commuting
test: «The train was crowded because so many people were commuting into the city.» What does commuting mean here? | Sleeping on a holiday | Buying tickets for the weekend | *Travelling regularly between home and work | Singing loudly on the platform
test: Which sentence uses commuting correctly? | *Her commute to school takes twenty minutes by bike. | The commute is a type of red biscuit. | We commuted yesterday, so the pie was hot. | The cat was commuting on the sofa all afternoon.
exam: In law, commuting a punishment means: | Forgetting it altogether | *Making it less severe | Making it stricter | Doubling it for the same crime
